# Building a passing grade
#
# Alice scored 7 and Bob scored 3; a score of at least 5 passes. A rule
# gives each passing student a grade written as a list, (:pass 7), holding
# the label and the score. Only Alice gets one. The example shows a numeric
# comparison built-in and a rule that builds a list in its conclusion.

@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#> .
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/assignment#> .

# The scores.
:alice :score 7 .
:bob :score 3 .

# A score of 5 or more earns the grade (:pass score).
{
    ?x :score ?score .
    ?score math:notLessThan 5 .
} => {
    ?x :grade (:pass ?score)
} .
